I have an idea about named weapons.  As it is right now, some named weapons
are pretty useless due to the abundant existence of more powerful ones.
Someone suggested making it more difficult or unlikely to find them.  The 
problem with is that if you don't have one, you'll have a very hard time 
with the game.  But once you find a good one or two, you really don't need 
any more, since weapons do not get 'used up' like potions and scrolls.  So 
here is what I propose.

While there exists at least one named weapon in the game, your god will not
grant you another one (other methods of obtaining named weapons, like 
wishing, remain unchanged).  Instead, what you can do is 'trade in'.  You
do this by putting a named weapon on a coalign-altar and #pray (all praying 
restrictions apply), sort of like potions of water.  Depending on your 
current luck and some random factors, a few things could happen:

1) Nothing happens
2) Your god takes back that weapon.
3) Your god takes back that weapon and gives another (named or normal) weapon
   in return.

In cases (2) and (3) the number of named weapons existing in the game should
change appropriately (for the purpose of wishing, for example).  Note that
there is a lot of risk involved.  You may lose the only named weapon that 
you have.  Or you may get a new weapon inferior to the old one.  You should,
however, be able to reduce this risk by improving your luck, making it more
likely that you'll get a better, named weapon (of course, someone has sit
down and ranks all the weapons, a very subjective process).

If someone has already proposed this before, then forgive my ignorance.
Otherwise, let me know what you think.


